  "description": "A 30-run Monte Carlo batch with requirements, a batch seed, outcome statistics and sensitivity. Template 25's satellite, half a day at 400 km: each run draws its orbit, drag coefficient (2.2 to 3.0) and dry mass (150 kg +/- 7.5 kg).\n\nWhat to look at:\n- Run it in Monte Carlo mode (the mode beside Run): about a minute in one process.\n- Requirements tab: R-ALT-01 (lowest altitude at least 389 km, 90 % confidence) is met: no run is below, and the bound, 0.074, is under the allowed 0.1.\n- R-DECAY-01 (at most 19 m of semi-major axis lost) has no allowed probability: 2 of 30 runs lose more, an estimate of 0.067 with a bound of 0.17.\n- Statistics: each outcome's percentiles and its distribution over the runs.\n- Sensitivity: the drag coefficient drives the decay (rank correlation about -0.9); the dry mass, 5 % 1-sigma, much less (about +0.3, which 30 runs can give by chance).\n- Export report... writes all of it, with the batch's provenance, as Markdown or JSON.\n\nTry changing:\n- The batch seed: other draws, so other counts.\n- Number of runs: with more runs the bound comes closer to the estimate.\n- Processes, for a shorter batch on a computer with several CPUs.\n\nNote:\n- The batch seed (37) gives the same draws every time, with one process or many.",
